ImageSharp.Drawing -- https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp.Drawing
  (Apache License 2.0, full text in LICENSE-APACHE)
  Copyright (c) Six Labors
  The triangle fill of the tight-mesh mask in src/sprite.ts is derived from
  ImageSharp.Drawing v1.0.0-beta15, the version AssetStudio fills sprite
  meshes with, so that the mask matches AssetStudio's to the pixel. It is a
  modified TypeScript translation of parts of:
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/ScanEdge.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/ScanEdgeCollection.Build.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/RasterizerExtensions.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/PolygonScanner.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Rasterization/ActiveEdgeList.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/InternalPath.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Shapes/Helpers/TopologyUtilities.cs
    src/ImageSharp.Drawing/Processing/Processors/Drawing/FillPathProcessor{TPixel}.cs
  Changes: translated from C# to TypeScript; cut down to filling one closed
  triangle without antialiasing, with the odd-even rule, into a 0/1 mask;
  the memory pools, sorting helpers and span types are replaced by arrays.
  That code is under the Apache License 2.0.

ImageSharp -- https://github.com/SixLabors/ImageSharp
  (Apache License 2.0, full text in LICENSE-APACHE)
  Copyright (c) Six Labors
  The variant-atlas resize in src/resize.ts is derived from ImageSharp
  v2.1.3, the version AssetStudio resizes a variant atlas with, so that the
  resized sprite matches AssetStudio's to the byte. It is a modified
  TypeScript translation of parts of:
    src/ImageSharp/Processing/Processors/Transforms/Resize/ResizeKernelMap.cs
    src/ImageSharp/Processing/Processors/Transforms/Resize/ResizeKernel.cs
    src/ImageSharp/Processing/Processors/Transforms/Resize/ResizeWorker.cs
    src/ImageSharp/Processing/Processors/Transforms/Resize/ResizeProcessor{TPixel}.cs
    src/ImageSharp/Processing/Processors/Transforms/Resamplers/BicubicResampler.cs
    src/ImageSharp/Common/Helpers/TolerantMath.cs
    src/ImageSharp/Common/Helpers/Numerics.cs
    src/ImageSharp/PixelFormats/PixelImplementations/Bgra32.cs
  Changes: translated from C# to TypeScript; cut down to the default bicubic
  resize of an RGBA image, computing only a crop of the result, with the
  scalar arithmetic only (no SIMD paths, no periodic kernel map); the memory
  pools, parallel row workers and span types are replaced by arrays.
  That code is under the Apache License 2.0.

The code derived from ImageSharp.Drawing and ImageSharp, and only that code,
is under the Apache License 2.0; the rest of this package is under the MIT
License (LICENSE).

